{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))['\"'$defs'\"']\nfor k in ['ClaimDraft','Grounding','CodeAnchor']:\n print(k,json.dumps(s.get(k),indent=2))\nPY\nnl -ba ../agent-source/rawnode.go | sed -n '314,355p'\nnl -ba ../agent-source/log_unstable.go | sed -n '125,166p'\"","aggregated_output":"ClaimDraft {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"A sourced requirement under explicit conditions, not the script for one experiment.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"kind\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"obligation\",\n        \"assumption\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Kind\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"concern\": {\n      \"default\": \"implementation_semantics\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"consensus_safety\",\n        \"bounded_liveness\",\n        \"implementation_semantics\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Concern\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"description\": {\n      \"description\": \"Required relation across applicable objects and contexts; keep test instance IDs and timings in the check unless they determine applicability\",\n      \"title\": \"Description\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"source_ids\": {\n      \"description\": \"Located materials; file kinds do not establish normative authority\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"scope\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Scope\"\n    },\n    \"pending\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Pending\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"grounding\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Grounding\",\n      \"default\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [],\n        \"binding_ids\": [],\n        \"derivation\": \"\",\n        \"applicability\": \"\",\n        \"unresolved\": [],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": []\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"id\",\n    \"kind\",\n    \"description\",\n    \"source_ids\",\n    \"scope\",\n    \"pending\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"ClaimDraft\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\nGrounding {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"source_ids\": {\n      \"description\": \"Exact IDs of acquired implementation source materials; not Behavior or Binding IDs\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"expectation_ids\": {\n      \"description\": \"Exact IDs of acquired materials supporting the expectation; not invented expectation labels. Explain normative applicability in derivation.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Expectation Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"binding_ids\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Binding Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"derivation\": {\n      \"default\": \"\",\n      \"description\": \"This component\\u2019s sourced reasoning; cite accepted IDs instead of repeating their full argument\",\n      \"title\": \"Derivation\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"applicability\": {\n      \"default\": \"\",\n      \"description\": \"Conditions for this component, including any added assumptions or omitted protections\",\n      \"title\": \"Applicability\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"unresolved\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Unresolved\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"conflicts\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Conflicts\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"alternatives\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Alternatives\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"title\": \"Grounding\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\nCodeAnchor {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"source_ids\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"boundary_complete\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Boundary Complete\"\n    },\n    \"kind\": {\n      \"default\": \"declaration\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"declaration\",\n        \"interface_member\",\n        \"callsite\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Kind\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"material_id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Material Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"start_line\": {\n      \"minimum\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Start Line\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"end_line\": {\n      \"minimum\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"End Line\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"symbol\": {\n      \"title\": \"Symbol\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"material_id\",\n    \"start_line\",\n    \"end_line\",\n    \"symbol\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"CodeAnchor\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n   314\t\t\t//\n   315\t\t\t// To prevent these kinds of problems, we also attach the current term to the\n   316\t\t\t// MsgStorageAppendResp (above). If the term has changed by the time the\n   317\t\t\t// MsgStorageAppendResp if returned, the response is ignored and the unstable\n   318\t\t\t// log is not truncated. The unstable log is only truncated when the term has\n   319\t\t\t// remained unchanged from the time that the MsgStorageAppend was sent to the\n   320\t\t\t// time that the MsgStorageAppendResp is received, indicating that no-one else\n   321\t\t\t// is in the process of truncating the stable log.\n   322\t\t\t//\n   323\t\t\t// However, this replaces a correctness problem with a liveness problem. If we\n   324\t\t\t// only attempted to truncate the unstable log when appending new entries but\n   325\t\t\t// also occasionally dropped these responses, then quiescence of new log entries\n   326\t\t\t// could lead to the unstable log never being truncated.\n   327\t\t\t//\n   328\t\t\t// To combat this, we attempt to truncate the log on all MsgStorageAppendResp\n   329\t\t\t// messages where the unstable log is not empty, not just those associated with\n   330\t\t\t// entry appends. This includes MsgStorageAppendResp messages associated with an\n   331\t\t\t// updated HardState, which occur after a term change.\n   332\t\t\t//\n   333\t\t\t// In other words, we set Index and LogTerm in a block that looks like:\n   334\t\t\t//\n   335\t\t\t//  if r.raftLog.hasNextOrInProgressUnstableEnts() { ... }\n   336\t\t\t//\n   337\t\t\t// not like:\n   338\t\t\t//\n   339\t\t\t//  if len(rd.Entries) > 0 { ... }\n   340\t\t\t//\n   341\t\t\t// To do so, we attach r.raftLog.lastIndex() and r.raftLog.lastTerm(), not the\n   342\t\t\t// (index, term) of the last entry in rd.Entries. If rd.Entries is not empty,\n   343\t\t\t// these will be the same. However, if rd.Entries is empty, we still want to\n   344\t\t\t// attest that this (index, term) is correct at the current term, in case the\n   345\t\t\t// MsgStorageAppend that contained the last entry in the unstable slice carried\n   346\t\t\t// an earlier term and was dropped.\n   347\t\t\t//\n   348\t\t\t// A MsgStorageAppend with a new term is emitted on each term change. This is\n   349\t\t\t// the same condition that causes MsgStorageAppendResp messages with earlier\n   350\t\t\t// terms to be ignored. As a result, we are guaranteed that, assuming a bounded\n   351\t\t\t// number of term changes, there will eventually be a MsgStorageAppendResp\n   352\t\t\t// message that is not ignored. This means that entries in the unstable log\n   353\t\t\t// which have been appended to stable storage will eventually be truncated and\n   354\t\t\t// dropped from memory.\n   355\t\t\t//\n   125\t\t}\n   126\t}\n   127\t\n   128\t// stableTo marks entries up to the entry with the specified (index, term) as\n   129\t// being successfully written to stable storage.\n   130\t//\n   131\t// The method should only be called when the caller can attest that the entries\n   132\t// can not be overwritten by an in-progress log append. See the related comment\n   133\t// in newStorageAppendRespMsg.\n   134\tfunc (u *unstable) stableTo(id entryID) {\n   135\t\tgt, ok := u.maybeTerm(id.index)\n   136\t\tif !ok {\n   137\t\t\t// Unstable entry missing. Ignore.\n   138\t\t\tu.logger.Infof(\"entry at index %d missing from unstable log; ignoring\", id.index)\n   139\t\t\treturn\n   140\t\t}\n   141\t\tif id.index < u.offset {\n   142\t\t\t// Index matched unstable snapshot, not unstable entry. Ignore.\n   143\t\t\tu.logger.Infof(\"entry at index %d matched unstable snapshot; ignoring\", id.index)\n   144\t\t\treturn\n   145\t\t}\n   146\t\tif gt != id.term {\n   147\t\t\t// Term mismatch between unstable entry and specified entry. Ignore.\n   148\t\t\t// This is possible if part or all of the unstable log was replaced\n   149\t\t\t// between that time that a set of entries started to be written to\n   150\t\t\t// stable storage and when they finished.\n   151\t\t\tu.logger.Infof(\"entry at (index,term)=(%d,%d) mismatched with \"+\n   152\t\t\t\t\"entry at (%d,%d) in unstable log; ignoring\", id.index, id.term, id.index, gt)\n   153\t\t\treturn\n   154\t\t}\n   155\t\tnum := int(id.index + 1 - u.offset)\n   156\t\tu.entries = u.entries[num:]\n   157\t\tu.offset = id.index + 1\n   158\t\tu.offsetInProgress = max(u.offsetInProgress, u.offset)\n   159\t\tu.shrinkEntriesArray()\n   160\t}\n   161\t\n   162\t// shrinkEntriesArray discards the underlying array used by the entries slice\n   163\t// if most of it isn't being used. This avoids holding references to a bunch of\n   164\t// potentially large entries that aren't needed anymore. Simply clearing the\n   165\t// entries wouldn't be safe because clients might still be using them.\n   166\tfunc (u *unstable) shrinkEntriesArray() {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The runner observed two stale term-2 responses leave node 3’s unstable offset at 3. A term-3 response from a HardState-only append advanced it to 4; later responses advanced it to 5, and application reached index 4. I’ll use this exploration to define a narrow stale-completion obligation, without treating it as formal property evidence.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_obligation.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v1.json'))\nfor a in m['activities']:a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:\n for k in ['established_by','consumed_by']:f.pop(k,None)\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='B_PERSIST_DISPATCH':b['produces_fact_ids'].append('F_APPEND_COMPLETION_MARKER')\n if b['id']=='B_STABLE_COMPLETION':\n  b['consumes_fact_ids'].append('F_APPEND_COMPLETION_MARKER')\n  b['unknowns']=['Response consumption after log replacement and overlapping snapshot completion needs separate history coverage.']\n if b['id']=='B_CONTEXT':\n  b['cross_activity_effects']['A6']='A higher raft term invalidates previously issued append-completion markers for entry stabilization. Step rejects their entry portion while preserving snapshot completion separately.'\nm['facts'].append(dict(id='F_APPEND_COMPLETION_MARKER',meaning='RawNode has issued a local append-completion marker identifying a captured raft term and last unstable entry index/log term. Issuance alone does not establish write completion; the caller may return it only after the associated ordered storage work completes.',identity={'owner':'MsgStorageAppendResp.To','append_context':'MsgStorageAppendResp.Term','entry':'MsgStorageAppendResp.Index and LogTerm','origin':'actual response attached to a RawNode-produced append message'},validity_context='Eligible for entry stabilization only in its captured raft term and when the entry identity still matches unstable state; snapshot completion has a distinct lifetime.',representation=['MsgStorageAppend.Responses containing MsgStorageAppendResp'],invalidators=['B_CONTEXT'],reinterpreters=[],durability='Volatile protocol marker; physical write completion is an external prerequisite, not guaranteed by issuance.',recovery='Not recovered as a marker after restart; new Ready production regenerates work from recovered state.',source_ids=['S_STORAGE_MSG','S_CONFIG','S_DISPATCH','S_UNSTABLE'],unknowns=['Snapshot-bearing responses are outside the initial focused proposition.','Identical tuples can be emitted by different append work items; an execution must independently identify their origin rather than correlate on tuple alone.']))\nPath('completion-map.json').write_text(json.dumps(m,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nq=dict(question='Can a locally produced append-completion marker from an earlier raft term remove unstable entries when consumed after a real authority transition, even if its entry index/log term still matches?',importance='Removing unstable entries on an obsolete storage context can make later reads depend on stable storage while older writes are still in flight. The selected requirement is the documented local context fence; a consensus divergence or crash-loss consequence requires additional replacement and endpoint evidence.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',source_ids=['S_COMPLETION_EXPECTATION','S_STABLE_EXPECTATION','S_STORAGE_MSG','S_DISPATCH','S_CONFIG'],participants=['RawNode raft owner','ordered local append worker'],objects=['MsgStorageAppendResp','unstable log prefix'],contexts=['AsyncStorageWrites enabled','response scheduling term versus receiving raft term','matching entry index/log term without snapshot'],event_paths=['RawNode Ready -> MsgStorageAppend -> completed ordered write -> delayed attached MsgStorageAppendResp -> RawNode.Step after election'],activity_classes=['A2'],behavior_ids=['B_PERSIST_DISPATCH','B_CONTEXT','B_STABLE_COMPLETION'],fact_ids=['F_APPEND_COMPLETION_MARKER'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B_PROPOSE':'Produces real log entries and self-support during elected leadership.','B_APPEND_FOLLOWER':'Produces real replicated entries at the observed follower.','B_APPLY':'Consumes stabilization-dependent application eligibility; final application progress is a control endpoint, not the selected safety requirement.','B_ENTRY':'Provides serialized RawNode ownership and public Step/Ready boundaries.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Step explicitly rejects lower-term entry completion; unstable.stableTo separately checks index/log term.','Fresh HardState-only append messages can re-attest older entry identities under the new raft term.','Exploration 636c2af3f67d4f8a9411831b57ddd982 observed these protections in a no-replacement history; this is construction guidance rather than formal Evidence.'],unknowns=['A formal correlated before/after comparison remains to be executed and reviewed.','No overwrite/ABA, disk crash, snapshot completion or consensus endpoint is covered by the initial history.'],priority=2,trigger_rationale='The acquired producer documentation explicitly distinguishes raft term from retained entry term. Exploration produced two stale markers whose index/log term still matched, plus a fresh-term HardState-only marker for that same entry identity. This permits a discriminating local check without fabricating critical state.')\nclaim=dict(id='C_STALE_APPEND_COMPLETION',kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='For an authentic snapshot-free local append-completion response generated in an earlier raft term and returned after its ordered append work has completed, consuming that response in a later raft term must not truncate the unstable entry prefix, even when its entry index and log term match the current unstable log.',source_ids=['S_COMPLETION_EXPECTATION','S_STABLE_EXPECTATION','S_CONFIG'],scope=dict(description='AsyncStorageWrites RawNode entry-completion consumption across increasing raft terms, with serialized state-machine access and contract-compliant ordered local append work.',assumptions=['Response was produced by the same RawNode instance and returned unchanged after its storage work completed.','No crash/restart of that instance between marker production and consumption.','Response has no